/* Error — the root of the failure sub-object hierarchy. Concrete errors
 * declare themselves from below with the mono arrow (`this < Error`), the
 * open-world direction: Error never enumerates them and never changes.
 * The mono verifies, it does not inherit: a sub-object must expose every
 * observation of the super — no `this < Error` compiles without `message`. */
place Error { message Text }
